ocesses\", \"t\": \"None\", \"et\": \"1:48pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:46pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"m\": \"Extreme temperatures disrupt molecular movement in living organisms: heat accelerates molecular motion and can denature proteins, while cold slows movement, reducing enzyme activity and membrane fluidity. Both extremes threaten cellular stability and survival.\", \"t\": \"1:48 PM\", \"et\": \"1:52pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:48pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"m\": \"Continuous repair and maintenance are the hidden engines of life—they prevent living organisms from collapsing under the constant wear and tear of existence. Every cell is like a busy factory, and without ongoing upkeep, the machinery would quickly break down. Here’s how it works:\", \"t\": \"1:52 PM\", \"et\": \"1:55pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:52pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"m\": \"Maintenance functions are the essential biological activities that keep an organism alive, stable, and functioning properly. They include processes like respiration, circulation, excretion, digestion, and regulation of body temperature. Unlike growth or reproduction, which are about expansion and continuation of species, maintenance functions focus on sustaining the internal environment of the organism.\", \"t\": \"1:55 PM\", \"et\": \"2:02pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:55pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}]}, \"dat\": \"2026-03-16\", \"day\": \"Monday\", \"sci\": {\"h\": [\"Started lesson: Metals and Non-metals - time: 11:37am\"], \"m\": null, \"t\": null, \"ai\": null, \"et\": \"5:44pm\", \"ln\": \"Carbon and its Compounds\", \"qm\": \"10/10\", \"st\": \"11:42am\", \"wt\": null, \"qet\": \"5:44pm\", \"qst\": \"4:46pm\", \"sub\": null, \"sessions\": [{\"et\": \"11:41am\", \"ln\": \"M