\"2:51pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"m\": \"Living organisms must carry out certain maintenance functions continuously to survive and remain stable. These include:\\n\\nNutrition – Obtaining food and breaking it down to release energy and raw materials for growth and repair.\\n\\nRespiration – Converting biochemical energy (like glucose) into usable energy (ATP) through metabolic processes.\\n\\nTransport – Moving nutrients, gases, and waste products within the organism (e.g., blood circulation in animals, vascular transport in plants).\", \"t\": \"2:57 PM\", \"et\": \"3:01pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"2:57pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"m\": \"Continuous repairing and maintaining are absolutely vital for the survival of living organisms because life is dynamic — cells and tissues are constantly exposed to wear, damage, and environmental stress. The implications include:\\n\\nSustained Functionality – Repair ensures that essential processes like respiration, circulation, and signaling continue without interruption.\\n\\nLongevity – By fixing damage and replacing worn-out components, organisms extend their lifespan and maintain health.\", \"t\": \"3:01 PM\", \"et\": \"3:03pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"3:01pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}]}, \"dat\": \"2026-03-20\", \"day\": \"Friday\", \"sci\": {\"h\": null, \"m\": null, \"t\": null, \"ai\": null, \"et\": \"5:21pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": \"10/10\", \"st\": \"5:07pm\", \"wt\": null, \"qet\": \"5:20pm\", \"qst\": \"5:07pm\", \"sub\": null, \"sessions\": [{\"et\": null, \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"2:46pm\", \"mde\": \"practice\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null}, {\"et\": \"5:21pm\", \"ln\": \"Life Processes\", \"qm\": \"10/10\", \"st\": \"5:07pm\", \"mde\": \"quiz\", \"qet\": \"5:20pm\", \"qst\": \"5:07pm\"}]}, \"smt\": {\"c\": 16, \"w\": 4, \"