\"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}, {\"m\": \"If Parliament does not sanction public money, the government cannot legally withdraw funds from the Consolidated Fund of India, halting its ability to spend on administration, welfare, and development. This creates a financial paralysis and often signals a loss of majority support, which can trigger a political crisis.\", \"t\": \"1:39 PM\", \"et\": \"1:47pm\", \"ln\": \"working of institutions\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:39pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}, {\"m\": \"rliament exercises control over government financial spending primarily through the annual budget process, grants and appropriation bills, and post-expenditure audits. This ensures that no money can be withdrawn from the Consolidated Fund of India without parliamentary approval, keeping the executive accountable to the legislature.\", \"t\": \"1:47 PM\", \"et\": \"1:53pm\", \"ln\": \"working of institutions\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:47pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}, {\"m\": \"The relationship between Parliament and public money is one of authority, accountability, and control. In India’s constitutional framework, Parliament is the ultimate guardian of how public funds are raised and spent. The executive (government) cannot spend a single rupee without Parliament’s sanction, making financial control a cornerstone of parliamentary democracy.\", \"t\": \"1:53 PM\", \"et\": \"1:56pm\", \"ln\": \"working of institutions\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"1:53pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}, {\"m\": \"Practice questions for Gravitation\", \"t\": \"None\", \"et\": \"4:57pm\", \"ln\": \"Gravitation\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"4:49pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"m\": \"6. time-None, Practice questions for events and processes\", \"t\": \"None\", \"et\": \"5:43pm\", \"ln\": \"events and processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"5:07pm\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}, {\"m\": \"7. time-5:11 PM, The Soviet government denied its citizens fundamental civil and political rights, including freedom of speech, freedom of religion, freedom of movement, and the right to independent political activity. These restrictions were enforced through censorship, repression, and the one-party system under the Communist Party.\", \"t\": \"5:11 PM\", \"et\": null, \"ln\": \"events and processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": null, \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}, {\"m\": \"8. time-5:24 PM, Socialist ideals strongly shaped anti-colonial movements by providing both an ideological framework and practical support. They emphasized equality, anti‑imperialism, and collective ownership, which resonated with colonized peoples seeking liberation from exploitative colonial systems. The Soviet Union and socialist movements worldwide actively backed decolonization struggles, linking them to the broader fight against capitalism.\", \"t\": \"5:24 PM\", \"et\": null, \"ln\": \"events and processes\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": null, \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": \"Social\"}]}, \"dat\": \"2026-04-01\", \"day\": \"Wednesday\", \"sci\": {\"h\": null, \"m\": null, \"t\": null, \"ai\": null, \"et\": null, \"ln\": \"Gravitation\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"4:49pm\", \"wt\": null, \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": null, \"sessions\": [{\"et\": \"3:45pm\", \"ln\": \"Motion\", \"qm\": \"9/10\", \"st\": \"2:47pm\", \"tm\": \"9/10\", \"mde\": \"quiz\", \"qet\": \"3:43pm\", \"qst\": \"2:47pm\", \"sub\": \"Science\"}, {\"et\": null, \"ln\": \"Gravitation\", \"qm\": null, \"st\": \"4:49pm\", \"mde\": \"practice\", \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null}]}, \"smt\": {\"h\": null, \"m\": null, \"t\": null, \"ai\": null, \"et\": null, \"ln\": null, \"qm\": null, \"st\": null, \"wt\": null, \"qet\": null, \"qst\": null, \"sub\": null}, \"soc\": {\"h\": [\"Started lesson: drainage - time: 1:23pm\"], \"m\": null, \"t\": null, \"ai\": null, \"et\